Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         git
Description: git reflog browser and reset preview
 gitrl-z shows the git reflog the way gitg shows commit history, and previews
 what a hard reset would do before you run it.
 .
 The reflog remembers where every branch has been, including commits that a
 rebase rewrote or a reset abandoned. gitrl-z lists it, and when an entry is
 selected it draws the commit graph as it would look if that entry's branch
 were reset there.
 .
 gitrl-z is read only: it never writes to the repository. It shows the command
 that would produce the previewed state, and running it stays your decision.
 The command line is gitrlz.
